on/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12f9fc63-1e5b-58f3-9165-48ecf337098a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324140} {:answer/id #uuid "6531f6ef-7836-5c36-8ad2-b64340ef2dd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324806} {:answer/id #uuid "716e8f1f-3359-5b9c-a2b5-8043eda079e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324907} {:answer/id #uuid "942d2637-f186-5cc3-808c-b7d930c541bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325234} {:answer/id #uuid "a0ddd36b-c315-54de-90f4-9ca1832ae646" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "942d2637-f186-5cc3-808c-b7d930c541bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325234} :answer-field/id #uuid "715194d1-fad4-5aa4-83e8-d5906bffa1a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326421}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e80c83a9-9107-528b-af57-73287d15e8e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-42061" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y+z=0 \\\\  & -4x+6y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n- The system has no solution\n- The system is consistent independent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 6 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 6 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we can to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."}]}
